usage: tetriz-connectors config put [flags]

Store an organization's connector config. A write with --credentials resets the connector's health, so a paused connector runs again. A write without it keeps the stored credentials and health, and a write without --settings keeps the stored settings.

Flags:
  -connector string
    	connector id, for example github (required)
  -credentials string
    	credentials JSON object; required on the first put, and kept from the stored config when omitted
  -disabled
    	store the config disabled
  -org string
    	organization id, a UUID (required)
  -settings string
    	settings JSON object; {} on the first put, and kept from the stored config when omitted
